SRR31143027	PRJNA1178722	SRP541656	SAMN44479622	SRX26524734	Homo sapiens	organoid, CRISPRa, DMSO, CROP-seq	organoid, CRISPRa, DMSO, CROP-seq	Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8599467: organoid, CRISPRa, DMSO, CROP-seq Homo sapiens RNA-Seq	RNA-Seq	TRANSCRIPTOMIC SINGLE CELL	cDNA	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina NovaSeq 6000	The organoids infected with the sgRNA library were dissociated into single cells, and the live cells were FACS sorted (BD FACS Aria2) to isolate them for single-cell RNA-seq Cells were prepared for single-cell RNA-seq using the 10X Chromium Controller and Chromium Single Cell 3' Library & Gel Bead Kit v2 (10x Genomics). From the final library, the sgRNA sequences are specifically amplified with PCR, as described before, with the following primers: 5'-AATGATACGGCGACCACCGAGATCTACAC-3' and 5'-CAAGCAGAAGACGGCATACGAGATCAGCCTCGGTCTCGTGGGCTCGGAGATGTGTATAAGAGACAGgtgttttgagactataaGtatcccttggagaaCCAcctTGTTG-3'. PCR cycling was performed according to the following protocol: (1) 95°C for 3 min, (2) 98°C for 15 s, then 70°C for 10 s (15 cycles) (3) 72 C for 1 min. The resulting sgRNA barcode library was purified via a 0.8X SPRI selection, and then further size was selected using BluePippin (Sage Science). sgRNA barcode libraries were sequenced as spike-ins alongside the parent RNA-seq libraries (5% spike-in) on a NovaSeq 6000, following the manufacturer's recommendations.	46491290	5532463510	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR311/027/SRR31143027/SRR31143027_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR311/027/SRR31143027/SRR31143027_2.fastq.gz	2f799d902be1679584671faaa691bfc4;d7ec308d6b7ef95db04b964e8fd89e13	1008727080;1013009946
